    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d930">

                <pb facs="0840" n="724" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg724"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2856.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-22T20:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 22, 1912—8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Situation in Sinaloa is graver; entire Culiacan district has risen. Consul
                    reports Americans being mistreated and robbed and have applied to the American
                    consul at Mazatlan (Alger) asking when, in the absence of protection by the
                    Mexican Government, they can expect it from the Government of the United States.
                    Consul has been notified of the sending of this telegram, and also instructed to
                    advise Americans where possible to remove to a place of safety. The American
                    interests in this section are very great in property, and I believe some
                    energetic action necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
